Oura Workout Alert
Last updated: October 19, 2026

Oura Workout Alert is a personal, non-commercial project used only by its creator, Isabelle.

What it accesses: workout data from the Oura API (activity type, time, duration, calories, distance and intensity). Nothing else.

How it's used: only to send the owner a notification about their own workouts and their progress against their weekly fitness goals.

Where it's stored: a small state file kept in a private GitHub repository. It holds the Oura login token and the IDs of workouts already notified about. Workout data is not stored long-term.

Sharing: data is never sold or shared. Notification text is sent through the ntfy.sh service to the owner's own phone.

Deleting data: revoke the app's access in your Oura account settings at any time. This stops all access immediately.

